---
import { Code } from "astro:components";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");

const example = `version: 0
ports:
  web: random
services:
  web:
    command: npm start
    env:
      PORT: \${{ ports.web }}
    ready:
      http: http://localhost:\${{ ports.web }}/healthz
test:
  sequence:
    - name: lint
      command: npm run lint
    - name: e2e
      command: npm run test:e2e`;
---

<Layout
  title="Home"
  description="Testfile — a declarative YAML format for running your project's tests."
  sidebar={false}
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-text">
      <h1>
        Testfile, the YAML way to describe your test setup and dependencies.
        <span class="grad">Run it locally and on the CI.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="lead">
        A YAML file that describes the whole test setup, with the services
        your tests depend on — which makes runs reproducible, on your
        machine and on CI. Every run is recorded, and even CI runs can be
        inspected locally.
      </p>
      <div class="cta">
        <a class="button primary" href={`${base}/docs/getting-started`}>Get started</a>
        <a class="button ghost" href={`${base}/docs/index`}>What is a Testfile?</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-code">
      <div class="window">
        <div class="titlebar">
          <span class="dot red"></span>
          <span class="dot blue"></span>
          <span class="dot plain"></span>
          <span class="fname">Testfile</span>
        </div>
        <Code code={example} lang="yaml" themes={{ light: "github-light", dark: "github-dark" }} />
      </div>
      <p class="run-hint"><code>testfile run</code> — that's the whole CI job.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="features">
    <div class="feature">
      <h3><span class="marker blue"></span>Simple definitions</h3>
      <p>
        The setup is easy: a name and a command is a test, and
        <a href={`${base}/docs/getting-started`}><code>testfile init</code></a>
        writes the first version for you. Plain YAML, validated by a
        schema, readable in every code review.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature">
      <h3><span class="marker red"></span>Scales with requirements</h3>
      <p>
        Grow from one command to sequences, parallel groups and
        <a href={`${base}/docs/matrix`}>matrix tests</a> — with retries,
        conditions and
        <a href={`${base}/docs/writing-tests#result-caching`}>result caching</a>
        when the suite gets big. The same file runs locally, in watch mode
        and on CI.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature">
      <h3><span class="marker blue"></span>Manages your services</h3>
      <p>
        A database — or any other
        <a href={`${base}/docs/services`}>service your tests need</a> — is
        declared once and started on demand, as a container or a plain
        process: health-checked before the first test runs and reachable
        through <a href={`${base}/docs/env-and-ports`}>random ports</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="viewer">
    <h2>Unified viewer for local and CI runs</h2>
    <p class="viewer-lead">
      Browse recorded runs in the terminal (<code>testfile-viewer tui</code>)
      or in the browser (<code>testfile-viewer serve</code>): statuses,
      durations, per-test logs, service logs — and <em>why</em> a test ran
      or came from the cache. A simple way to sync runs between machines,
      including <a href={`${base}/docs/github-action`}>CI runs</a> on your
      computer, like GitHub Actions.
    </p>
    <div class="shot">
      <img
        src={`${base}/screenshots/viewer.png`}
        alt="The Testfile web viewer showing a recorded run: the runs table, per-test statuses with cache reasons, a service row and the merged log"
        width="1280"
        height="660"
        loading="lazy"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="all-features">
    <h2>Everything in the box</h2>
    <div class="feature-groups">
      <div class="group">
        <h3>The format</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Nested tests: <a href={`${base}/docs/writing-tests#sequences`}>sequences</a> and <a href={`${base}/docs/writing-tests#parallel-groups`}>parallel groups</a></li>
          <li><a href={`${base}/docs/matrix`}>Matrix expansion</a> across versions and variants</li>
          <li><a href={`${base}/docs/writing-tests#conditional-tests`}>Conditions</a>, <a href={`${base}/docs/writing-tests#tags`}>tags</a> and per-test <a href={`${base}/docs/writing-tests#timeouts-env-workdir`}>timeouts</a></li>
          <li><a href={`${base}/docs/writing-tests#retries`}>Retries</a> and tolerated failures</li>
          <li><a href={`${base}/docs/writing-tests#setup-and-teardown`}>Setup &amp; teardown</a> hooks, DAG ordering with <code>needs</code></li>
          <li><a href={`${base}/docs/writing-tests#composing-testfiles`}>Includes</a> for monorepos</li>
          <li><a href={`${base}/docs/env-and-ports#templates`}>Template expressions</a> with defaults</li>
          <li><a href="https://github.com/christoph-jerolimov/testfile/blob/main/schema/testfile.schema.json">JSON schema</a> validation &amp; editor autocompletion</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="group">
        <h3>Services &amp; environment</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Processes or containers (podman/docker) as <a href={`${base}/docs/services`}>services</a></li>
          <li>Readiness by HTTP, TCP, log line or command</li>
          <li><a href={`${base}/docs/env-and-ports`}>Random ports</a> for parallel-safe runs</li>
          <li>Services shared across matrix instances</li>
          <li><a href={`${base}/docs/env-and-ports#an-isolated-environment`}>Isolated environment</a> with explicit <code>forwardEnv</code></li>
          <li><a href={`${base}/docs/env-and-ports#env-files-and-secrets`}>Env files</a> with secret masking</li>
          <li>Graceful teardown, also on Ctrl+C</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="group">
        <h3>Running &amp; CI</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><a href={`${base}/docs/cli#filtering`}>Filters</a> by name, tag or matrix value</li>
          <li>Re-run what broke (<code>--failed</code>) or what <a href={`${base}/docs/writing-tests#change-based-selection`}>changed</a></li>
          <li><a href={`${base}/docs/writing-tests#result-caching`}>Result caching</a> with <code>inputs</code></li>
          <li><a href={`${base}/docs/cli#watch-mode`}>Watch mode</a> and cache-aware <code>--dry-run</code></li>
          <li><a href={`${base}/docs/cli#machine-readable-reports`}>JUnit &amp; JSON reports</a>, collected <a href={`${base}/docs/writing-tests#artifacts`}>artifacts</a></li>
          <li><a href={`${base}/docs/github-action`}>GitHub Action</a> with PR annotations &amp; job summary</li>
          <li><a href={`${base}/docs/cli#the-tui`}>TUI</a>, <a href={`${base}/docs/cli#the-web-viewer`}>web viewer</a> and <a href={`${base}/docs/cli#tags`}>tag inventory</a></li>
          <li>Flaky-test detection, run diffs, <a href={`${base}/docs/cli#sharing-runs`}>run sharing</a> via S3 or GitHub</li>
          <li>VS Code extension and shell completions</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="all-features-cta">
      <a class="button ghost" href={`${base}/docs/writing-tests`}>Read the docs</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.05fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 3rem;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 3rem 0 1rem;
  }
  .hero h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 2.7vw, 2.2rem);
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .grad {
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--accent), var(--accent-red));
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    background-clip: text;
    color: transparent;
  }
  .lead {
    margin: 1.1rem 0 1.6rem;
    font-size: 1.06rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .cta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }
  .button {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.55rem 1.15rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
  }
  .button.primary {
    background: var(--accent);
    color: #ffffff;
  }
  .button.primary:hover {
    filter: brightness(1.1);
  }
  .button.ghost {
    border-color: var(--border);
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .button.ghost:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent);
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .window {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 12px 32px rgba(9, 105, 218, 0.08);
    background: var(--code-bg);
  }
  .titlebar {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    padding: 0.6rem 0.9rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .dot {
    width: 0.7rem;
    height: 0.7rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
  }
  .dot.red {
    background: var(--accent-red);
  }
  .dot.blue {
    background: var(--accent);
  }
  .dot.plain {
    background: var(--border);
  }
  .fname {
    margin-left: 0.4rem;
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .window :global(pre) {
    margin: 0;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 0;
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
  .run-hint {
    margin: 0.8rem 0 0;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .features {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    padding: 2.5rem 0 1rem;
  }
  .feature {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem;
    background: var(--code-bg);
  }
  .feature h3 {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.55rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font-size: 1.02rem;
  }
  .marker {
    width: 0.6em;
    height: 0.6em;
    border-radius: 2px;
    flex: none;
  }
  .marker.blue {
    background: var(--accent);
  }
  .marker.red {
    background: var(--accent-red);
  }
  .feature p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.93rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .viewer {
    padding: 2.5rem 0 1rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .viewer h2 {
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 2.4vw, 1.8rem);
  }
  .viewer-lead {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0 auto 1.75rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .shot {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 16px 40px rgba(9, 105, 218, 0.1);
  }
  .shot img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  .all-features {
    padding: 3rem 0 1rem;
  }
  .all-features h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 2.4vw, 1.8rem);
  }
  .feature-groups {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem 2rem;
  }
  .group h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.4rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .group ul {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    font-size: 0.93rem;
  }
  .group li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
    margin: 0.4rem 0;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .group li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.55em;
    width: 0.4em;
    height: 0.4em;
    border-radius: 1px;
    background: var(--accent);
  }
  .group:nth-child(2) li::before {
    background: var(--accent-red);
  }
  .all-features-cta {
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    text-align: center;
  }

  @media (max-width: 56rem) {
    .hero {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 2rem;
      padding-top: 1.5rem;
    }
    .features,
    .feature-groups {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
